{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":501552,"name":"Pratim Majumder","username":"ExploiTR","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/exploitr/{size}/122164_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-26T11:06:00.876Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501552-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501552-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501552-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501552-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot on Linux changes my XDG default \u003ccode\u003etext/html\u003c/code\u003e handler to \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot.desktop\u003c/code\u003e every time I launch it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI use Brave as my default browser:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003exdg-mime default brave-browser.desktop text/html\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore launching Grok, \u003ccode\u003exdg-open https://example.com\u003c/code\u003e correctly opens Brave. After launching Grok, \u003ccode\u003etext/html\u003c/code\u003e becomes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003etext/html=grok-bot.desktop\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eand \u003ccode\u003exdg-open\u003c/code\u003e opens Grok instead.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow can I prevent Grok Bot from registering itself as the default HTML handler while keeping its \u003ccode\u003egrokbot://\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003esand://\u003c/code\u003e handlers?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501552-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501552-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSet Brave as the default browser:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003exdg-mime default brave-browser.desktop text/html\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVerify:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003exdg-mime query default text/html\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n→ \u003ccode\u003ebrave-browser.desktop\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRun:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003exdg-open https://example.com\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n→ Opens in Brave.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaunch Grok Bot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCheck the MIME association again:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003exdg-mime query default text/html\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n→ \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot.desktop\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRun:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003exdg-open https://example.com\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n→ Opens in Grok Bot instead of Brave.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501552-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501552-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot should not modify the system’s default \u003ccode\u003etext/html\u003c/code\u003e handler when launched.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003etext/html\u003c/code\u003e should remain associated with the user’s selected browser, in my case \u003ccode\u003ebrave-browser.desktop\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot should only register and use its own handlers:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ex-scheme-handler/grokbot\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ex-scheme-handler/sand\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501552-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501552-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLinux\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501552-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501552-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion: 0.57.1\u003cbr\u003e\nBuilt: 2026-09-18T22:09:17.394Z\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: linux\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501552-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501552-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-26T14:54:21.127Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":30.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173050,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-hijacks-xdg-text-html-default-handler-on-linux","display_username":"Pratim Majumder","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139884,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-hijacks-xdg-text-html-default-handler-on-linux/173050/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":501648,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-26T14:54:30.147Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/exploitr\"\u003e@ExploiTR\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the report!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou’re right, Grok Bot shouldn’t touch your text/html default. It happens when Grok Bot registers its grokbot:// and sand:// links on startup. On GNOME-based desktops (GNOME, Cinnamon, MATE), the system tool it uses for that also sets the app as the HTML handler. This is a known issue and I’ve added your report to it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the meantime, you can restore Brave after Grok Bot has started:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003exdg-mime default brave-browser.desktop text/html\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you’d rather not do that by hand, a small launcher script that starts Grok Bot, waits a few seconds, and then runs that command will keep Brave as your default. The grokbot:// and sand:// links will keep working either way.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-26T14:54:30.147Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173050,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-hijacks-xdg-text-html-default-handler-on-linux","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-hijacks-xdg-text-html-default-handler-on-linux/173050/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":501719,"name":"Pratim Majumder","username":"ExploiTR","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/exploitr/{size}/122164_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:30:59.746Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi, thanks for the information. This is what I’m following for now. Hopefully the issue can be fixed in Grok Bot so it doesn’t overwrite the existing \u003ccode\u003etext/html\u003c/code\u003e association. I’ve edited the Grok bot shortcut itself so I don’t need a separate script.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-26T15:36:09.500Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173050,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-hijacks-xdg-text-html-default-handler-on-linux","display_username":"Pratim Majumder","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":87436,"username":"Colin","name":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139884,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-hijacks-xdg-text-html-default-handler-on-linux/173050/8","rea